}

record raw-autotune.work.midtone-shadow-contrast-versus-reference-renderers/1 : work {
    title "Midtone/shadow contrast: why our curve sits ~2x above reference renderers below the highlight end"
    state proposed
    scope [ path "src/analyze.rs", path "src/tone.rs" ]
    intent """
        Decide whether the view transform's midtone and shadow placement should carry more contrast, using _DSC1289 as the entry case and the full corpus as the gate. This is a default-affecting tone question, deliberately separated from the highlight chromaticity work, which is opt-in and cannot move unattended output.

        Entry observation. On _DSC1289 the rendered highlight end matches Windows Photo Viewer's render of the same ARW within 2 percent (p95 210.5 against 214.9) while every lower percentile sits about twice as high (p50 92.1 against 49.4, p25 57.9 against 29.3, p05 29.4 against 14.3). The visible consequence the user reported is that genuine veiling flare around sky-backlit foliage becomes conspicuous: the flare itself is in the capture and is relatively weaker than Windows' (near/far 1.144 against 1.172), but our lifted midtones put it on display.

        What is already ruled out. Not highlight reconstruction, sharpening, or chroma denoise: each was ablated and the near/far foliage gradient was unchanged. Not the automatic exposure: sidecar target_median_ev -0.23569 agrees with the embedded preview oracle's center_weighted_key_display_ev -0.27450 to 0.04 EV, so the camera would place the subject where we place it. Do not re-open either without new evidence.

        Where the mechanism lives. src/tone.rs owns the hue-preserving, middle-gray-anchored view transform; the per-frame parameters recorded for this file are black_input_ev -3.85744, white_input_ev 4.79819, black_output_ev -7.22882, white_output_ev 2.45213, exposure_ev 1.03732, with analysis key_score -0.28211, tonal_class normal, measured_dynamic_range_ev 7.85563, center_median_ev -1.02991. The shadow rolloff and the input-to-output EV mapping are the levers; exposure_ev is not.

        Why this needs care, not a quick fix. The curve is the product's look and applies to every frame by default, so CLAUDE.md's regression gate applies in full: a --dry-run --summary field-by-field diff over the corpus, cargo test --release, clippy, and --jobs 8 determinism. Any change must be justified against paired camera JPEGs across the corpus rather than one backlit frame, because more contrast will crush shadow detail on night and interior frames where the current placement was paired-validated. Windows Photo Viewer is a reference point, not ground truth: it is one vendor's aesthetic, and the project already records that camera JPEGs include creative rendering.

        First steps when picked up. Reproduce the percentile comparison across the paired-JPEG corpus, not just _DSC1289, and establish whether the ~2x midtone lift is systematic or specific to high-dynamic-range backlit scenes. If systematic, the question is the curve's shadow placement; if scene-dependent, it is the analyzer's target/contrast selection for this tonal class. Only then propose a change.
        """
    derived_from [ @raw-autotune.evidence.backlit-foliage-glow-is-exposure-20260810/2 ]
}

record raw-autotune.work.night-low-light-rendering/1 : work {
    title "Night / low-light rendering: raw detection, HDR-at-night local tone, noise-aware luma denoise"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "src/analyze.rs",
        path "src/api.rs",
        path "src/cli.rs",
        path "src/localtone.rs",
        path "src/luma.rs",
        path "src/main.rs",
        path "src/pipeline.rs",
        path "src/types.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        Substantially improve night/low-light rendering, on explicit user direction. Three coordinated additions, each inert (byte-identical) on clean daytime frames and fully deterministic.

        (1) DETECTION. A per-frame low_light_score in src/analyze.rs that fuses scene median darkness (p50_ev) with sensor noise (snr10_ev) and ISO, recorded in AnalysisStats and the sidecar (schema bump). The existing shape-based tonal_class does not capture absolute low light: the eight night pairs (ISO 6400-12800, p50 -2.8..-4.7 EV, snr10 about -0.9 EV) classify as Normal/HighDynamicRange, and daytime _DSC1275 (ISO 2500, f/18, bright ambient) has p50 -6.47 EV, so darkness or ISO alone mislead. Darkness AND noise must agree.

        (2) HDR-AT-NIGHT. Make the existing edge-aware single-frame local tone operator (src/localtone.rs build_hdr) automatic when low_light_score is high, at a strength scaled by it, to normalize/compress bright light sources and locally lift shadows while retaining local contrast. Per the user: do NOT globally lift contrast or exposure just because the scene is dark; the effect must be local. The global exposure controller is left untouched, honouring the controller freeze in docs/REVIEW-2026-07-30.md.

        (3) LUMA DENOISE. A new src/luma.rs: a noise-aware, self-guided, edge-preserving luminance denoiser scaled by snr10_ev (like chroma denoise but gentler, blend capped, worked in the log2-EV domain so the noisier shadows are cleaned hardest). It runs after analysis, so the exposure decision is byte-identical, and before the tone map and render, so the locally lifted shadows are not grainy. Empirically the current ISO 12800 renders carry heavy luma grain at 100% that the camera removes while chroma noise is already clean; the limitations string already admits luma noise is not reduced.

        Research basis: NPLIE (research/Illumination-estimation-...pdf) adaptive illumination adjustment I_f = I^log(I), a nature-preserving spatially varying gain that lifts shadows and preserves/compresses highlights; and the adaptive-gamma / Lite-ZeroDCE paper (research/An-adaptive-Correction-...pdf), scene-mean-driven adaptive correction with colour-constancy and well-exposedness objectives.

        Keeps every other constraint from raw-autotune.requirement.constraints-and-non-goals: byte-identical when off, --dry-run --summary diff ignores only elapsed_ms, determinism under --jobs 8, no earlier clamp, no HDR output container (this is tone mapping, not PQ/gain-map), and --highlight-contrast stays diagnostic.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
    source {
        kind external
        path "research/An-adaptive-Correction-Deep-Learning-based-Zero-Reference-Approach-for-Low-Light-Images.pdf"
        excerpt """
            Set the gamma parameter based on the average intensity of an image ... The gamma value is kept small for a low-light image with very poor overall brightness.
            """
    }
    source {
        kind external
        path "research/Illumination-estimation-for-nature-preserving-low-light-image-enhancement.pdf"
        excerpt """
            The proposed illumination adjustment is given as: I_f = I^log(I) ... The adaptive illumination adjustment improves the lightness of dark-regions and restricts the lightness of regions with normal illumination.
            """
    }
}

record raw-autotune.work.night-low-light-rendering/2 : work {
    title "Night / low-light rendering: raw detection, HDR-at-night local tone, noise-aware luma denoise"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "src/analyze.rs",
        path "src/api.rs",
        path "src/cli.rs",
        path "src/localtone.rs",
        path "src/luma.rs",
        path "src/main.rs",
        path "src/pipeline.rs",
        path "src/types.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        Substantially improve night/low-light rendering, on explicit user direction. Three coordinated additions, each inert (byte-identical) on clean daytime frames and fully deterministic.

        (1) DETECTION. A per-frame low_light_score in src/analyze.rs fuses scene median darkness (p50_ev), sensor noise (snr10_ev/ISO), and a physical ambient-light gate (capture_ev100 derived from shutter, aperture, and ISO), recorded in AnalysisStats and the sidecar (schema bump). The shape-based tonal_class does not capture absolute low light. Darkness and noise alone also do not suffice: the daylight waterfall stress frames _DSC1277/_DSC1278 are deliberately dark raw captures at ISO 8000-10000 and previously scored 0.87-0.96, but their f/18, 1/1600 s exposures are 12.3-12.7 EV100. Automatic night tone must require darkness AND noise AND low capture EV when complete exposure metadata is available, with the former two-cue decision retained as a fallback when metadata is incomplete. This is physical capture classification, not semantic scene detection.

        (2) HDR-AT-NIGHT. Make the existing edge-aware single-frame local tone operator (src/localtone.rs build_hdr) automatic when low_light_score is high, at a strength scaled by it, to normalize/compress bright light sources and locally lift shadows while retaining local contrast. Per the user: do NOT globally lift contrast or exposure just because the scene is dark; the effect must be local. The global exposure controller is left untouched, honouring the controller freeze in docs/REVIEW-2026-07-30.md.

        (3) LUMA DENOISE. A new src/luma.rs: a noise-aware, self-guided, edge-preserving luminance denoiser scaled by snr10_ev (like chroma denoise but gentler, blend capped, worked in the log2-EV domain so the noisier shadows are cleaned hardest). It runs after analysis, so the exposure decision is byte-identical, and before the tone map and render, so the locally lifted shadows are not grainy. Empirically the current ISO 12800 renders carry heavy luma grain at 100% that the camera removes while chroma noise is already clean; the limitations string already admits luma noise is not reduced.

        Research basis: NPLIE (research/Illumination-estimation-...pdf) adaptive illumination adjustment I_f = I^log(I), a nature-preserving spatially varying gain that lifts shadows and preserves/compresses highlights; and the adaptive-gamma / Lite-ZeroDCE paper (research/An-adaptive-Correction-...pdf), scene-mean-driven adaptive correction with colour-constancy and well-exposedness objectives.

        Keeps every other constraint from raw-autotune.requirement.constraints-and-non-goals: byte-identical when off, --dry-run --summary diff ignores only elapsed_ms, determinism under --jobs 8, no earlier clamp, no HDR output container (this is tone mapping, not PQ/gain-map), and --highlight-contrast stays diagnostic.
        """
    acceptance {
        check build-tests-and-lints-pass {
            statement """
                The release test suite and release clippy pass after the EV100 detector refinement.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test --release && cargo clippy --lib --bins --release -- -D warnings"
            verified_by [ @raw-autotune.evidence.night-ev100-build-tests-20260813/1 ]
        }
        check day-night-tone-is-inert {
            statement """
                A high-ISO daylight frame renders byte-identically with night tone enabled or disabled, while a confirmed night frame changes.
                """
            method command
            command "sha256sum .agent/scratch/night-day-ev100-pixels/day-{on,off}/_DSC1277_auto.jpg .agent/scratch/night-day-ev100-pixels/night-{on,off}/_DSC1310_auto.jpg"
            verified_by [ @raw-autotune.evidence.night-day-tone-pixel-gate-20260813/1 ]
        }
        check night-day-detector-separates-corpus {
            statement """
                The eight night positives remain above the automatic tone threshold while the five hostile high-ISO daylight negatives score zero through the physical EV100 gate.
                """
            method command
            command "jq -r '.files[] | [(.input|split(\"/\")|last), .analysis.capture_ev100, .analysis.low_light_score] | @tsv' .agent/scratch/night-day-ev100-gate-20260813.json"
            verified_by [ @raw-autotune.evidence.night-day-ev100-separation-20260813/1 ]
        }
        check night-render-improves {
            statement """
                Detected night frames receive useful local tone compression and noise-aware luma cleanup without a global exposure lift.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @raw-autotune.evidence.night-low-light-render-improvement-20260810/1 ]
        }
    }
    supersedes [ @raw-autotune.work.night-low-light-rendering/1 ]
}

