record raw-autotune.work.slice-8-local-tone-sky-ground-hdr-evaluation/2 : work {
    title "Slice 8 — Sky stage attribution and local-tone/HDR evaluation"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "src/localtone.rs", path "src/tone.rs", path "tools/**" ]
    intent """
        Attribute the visible sky failure to an exact pipeline boundary before changing the default render. Keep the existing local-tone and HDR evaluations for scene-luminance compression, but do not use either operator to conceal a colour-estimation discontinuity.

        Add renderer-exact, lossless diagnostic checkpoints after the tone curve, chroma scale, highlight white mix, and gamut compression. The normal render and the final diagnostic checkpoint must share one implementation and remain byte-identical. On `_DSC1289.ARW`, compare the default against reconstruction disabled, `--local-tone 0.35`, and `--hdr 0.5`; measure adjacent OKLab chroma steps across raw clip-state boundaries and within the same clip state.

        The current attribution found that reconstruction introduces clip-cohort plateaus and that the max-channel-weighted tone shoulder is the main discontinuity amplifier. Local tone and HDR do not repair the colour estimate, gamut compression is effectively inactive in the measured sky, and the peak-preserving path toward white reduces rather than creates the boundary. Continue evaluating local tone/HDR only after the reconstruction estimator and its end-to-end ground-truth bench can distinguish recovered detail from invented colour.
        """
    note """
        On the bright upper-sky crop of `_DSC1289.ARW`, the p90 adjacent OKLab a/b step at a clip-state boundary was 0.00423 after highlight reconstruction and 0.01922 immediately after the tone curve (4.5x). It was 0.01612 in the final default render, versus 0.00313 with reconstruction disabled. `--local-tone 0.35` measured 0.01618 and `--hdr 0.5` measured 0.01663. Gamut pre/post p90 was unchanged. The frame contained 344,861 two-or-more-channel clipped pixels and no three-channel-clipped pixels under the current classifier, so its small white patch is estimator neutralisation plus tone mapping rather than a region with all three raw channels classified clipped.
        """
    acceptance {
        check local-tone-hdr-remain-colour-neutral {
            statement """
                Local-tone or HDR promotion is decided on luminance separation and halo behaviour only after highlight colour continuity passes the ground-truth reconstruction gate.
                """
            method command
        }
        check renderer-exact-stage-attribution {
            statement """
                Lossless checkpoints use the production renderer's exact arithmetic, leave the normal output byte-identical, and isolate the first stage that materially amplifies clip-boundary colour steps.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @raw-autotune.evidence.sky-stage-attribution-20260809/1 ]
        }
    }
    supersedes [ @raw-autotune.work.slice-8-local-tone-sky-ground-hdr-evaluation/1 ]
    source {
        kind legacy
        path ".agents/plans/2026-08-07-white-blowout-testing-apparatus.md"
        excerpt """
            - **Owns:** `src/localtone.rs`, `src/tone.rs` exposure-gain path, `tools/` evaluation.
            - **Does:** sweep existing Gaussian-surround operator at `--local-tone 0.35` (advice) with the new uncertainty gating; measure sky-band vs ground-band EV separation, halo around foliage/ridge, `HIGHLIGHT_NORM` interaction, and `docs/HDR_EVALUATION.md` unclipped-headroom figure. If warranted, implement the guided-filter log-luminance `B=guided(L), D=L-B, ΔEV = B_compressed + kD - L` design from advice §"Where HDR belongs" with median-correction≈0, shadow +0.4-0.6 EV, highlight −0.6-0.9 EV, single scalar RGB gain. Gate: do not ship default-on until halo test passes on leaf/branch/ridge crops.
            - **Depends on:** Slice 7.
            """
    }
}

